## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical integration of OpenAI with security tooling, automation, and multi-tenant isolation, plus safety controls (PII redaction, auditing) and deployment practices (canary rollout).

## Key Concepts
- OpenAI integration with Defender for Cloud and CI/CD tooling
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search on Azure Blob
- Per-tenant state in Cosmos DB; secret management via Key Vault
- Azure Automation or IaC task generation for remediation
- PII redaction, Data Lake auditing, API Management canary

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: ingest alerts, ground to KB, generate remediation, dispatch runbook
async function handleIncident(tenantId, alert) {
  const kb = await loadKB(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(alert, kb);
  const guidance = await openai.complete(prompt);
  if (validate(guidance)) {
    const runbook = generateRunbook(guidance);
    await dispatchRunbook(runbook, tenantId);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout and measure safety/latency impact?
- What failure modes require fallback behavior and how would you implement it?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests secure, compliant Azure OpenAI usage for security incidents, focusing on input redaction, tenant isolation, and auditable data paths.

## Key Concepts
- Azure API Management, Functions, Key Vault
- Text Analytics redaction, data privacy
- Cognitive Search grounding against versioned KB in Blob
- Structured JSON playbooks and audit logging

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactInput(text, patterns){
  let out = text;
  for (const p of patterns){
    const re = new RegExp(p, 'g');
    out = out.replace(re, '[REDACTED]');
  }
  return out;
}
```

